<section class="summary">
  <div class="wrap summary-grid">
    <p class="lede">
      MCP's transport writes to the raw Node socket, so most of the design is about getting
      the raw request down to it and keeping Koa or Express from writing over it afterwards —
      then handing each session its own isolated server, bound to the user who opened it.
    </p>
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat"><strong>2</strong><span>transports: Koa &amp; Express</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>1:1</strong><span>session ↔ McpServer, never shared</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>TypeBox</strong><span>schemas, converted to Zod at the SDK boundary</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .summary {
    padding: 48px 0 8px;
  }

  .summary-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 32px;
  }

  .lede { max-width: 46ch; }

  .stat-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 30px;
  }

  .stat strong {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    color: var(--gold);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .stat span {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .summary-grid { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }
</style>
